    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s strongest plays today center on high-leverage matchups against vulnerable pitching, headlined by **Bryce Harper** (72.33) and **Cal Raleigh** (72.28). **Bryce Harper** draws an excellent matchup against E-Rod, benefiting from a +14% SP Skill bump and a solid xwOBA of 0.394, making him our premier anchor. Meanwhile, **Cal Raleigh** possesses the day's highest ceiling due to a soft matchup against Paez (9.12 xERA); the park factors and SP deficiency align perfectly for a multi-HR potential outing. **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) also warrants attention as a high-upside play, bolstered by a +14% park factor and +17% SP Skill advantage, solidifying our outfield core.\n\nWhile our starters are set, the most difficult sit-start decision involved navigating the lower tier of our utility depth. **Jung Hoo Lee** (43.07) remained in the lineup despite a sub-50 score, primarily because of the extreme scarcity of stolen bases in this league. While his projection is suppressed by a brutal matchup against the elite Skenes, his sprint speed and situational utility narrowly beat out the rest of the bench. We are tracking a major risk factor with **Jung Hoo Lee** today, as the combination of Skenes\u2019 3.18 xERA and a sub-2.0s pop time from the opposing catcher severely limits our SB efficiency. Elsewhere, **Gleyber Torres** (45.32) and **Yainer Diaz** (46.02) are functioning strictly as floor plays; both are held back by suboptimal platoon splits, but their presence is necessary to maintain our active game caps as we approach the final month of the season. \n\nWe continue to monitor the status of **Will Smith** and **Matt Chapman**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our late-game tactical flexibility. As always, players like **Justin Crawford** and **Tyler Freeman** remain strictly in the \"depth\" category\u2014**Justin Crawford** lacks a clear path to playing time today, and **Tyler Freeman** continues his stint in the minors, rendering them non-factors for this slate. Keep a close watch on **Alex Freeland** (50.49), whose value is almost entirely driven by an SP Skill bump; if his defensive positioning or order rank shifts prior to first pitch, he remains our most volatile asset on the diamond.",
